From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slothfulchat <patches@slothfulchat.invalid>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 15:24:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] web-app: requests link in the chat list, quiet group requests

Request the chat list with core's DC_GCL_NO_REQUESTS so contact requests
no longer get their own rows. Core's requests link is rendered by the
archive-link component (forum icon, "Requests" label, the request count
as its counter and in its aria-label, no context menu); clicking it opens
a "Requests" view that reuses the archive view's header (back button and
title) and lists the chats via the `is:request` query. The unread filter
does not apply inside that view. Once the view is empty, e.g. after
accepting the last request, it says so instead of showing a blank list.
"Requests" and the empty note are untranslated strings for now; there is
no plural of chat_request_label upstream.

The bundle runs the published @deltachat/jsonrpc-client, which predates
core/0036, so DC_GCL_NO_REQUESTS, DC_CHAT_ID_REQUESTS_LINK and the
RequestsLink item type are defined in ChatListHelpers rather than read
from `C` (where they would be undefined at runtime).

Opening a chat switches to the list it lives in, so a request opened
from a notification shows in the Requests view and a normal chat opened
from there returns to the normal list; this is keyed on the chat id, so
accepting the open request stays in the Requests view. Keyboard
next/previous chat and "select first chat" skip every special chat ID.

Notifications for group contact requests are dropped in
flushNotifications (one getBasicChatInfo per chat; a failed lookup no
longer aborts the flush). 1:1 requests still notify: missing a real
first message is worse than one ping.
